menu "Little World startup"

    choice LW_BOOT_MODE
        prompt "Startup mode"
        default LW_BOOT_MODE_OS_V2
        help
            Selects which UI the firmware starts after board bring-up.
            OS V2 is the integrated desktop; Legacy keeps the pre-OS shell.

        config LW_BOOT_MODE_OS_V2
            bool "OS V2 desktop (lw_os_start)"
        config LW_BOOT_MODE_LEGACY
            bool "Legacy application shell (lw_ui_start)"
    endchoice

    config LW_ENABLE_AUDIO
        bool "Probe the ES8311 speaker path at boot"
        default y
        help
            Opens the BSP speaker codec so volume changes can reach the
            hardware. When the codec is absent the OS keeps the volume as a
            stored preference and the UI must not claim real audio output.

endmenu
menu "Little World connectivity"

    config LW_NET_WIFI_ENABLE
        bool "Enable the ESP32-C6 Wi-Fi backend"
        default n
        help
            Compile the real Wi-Fi adapter (lw_net_wifi_esp.c) and pull in
            esp_wifi. Requires the esp_hosted and esp_wifi_remote managed
            components and a working SDIO link to the C6. When disabled the
            firmware reports the radio as unsupported instead of pretending
            to scan.

    config LW_NET_SNTP_ENABLE
        bool "Enable SNTP time synchronisation"
        default n
        depends on LW_NET_WIFI_ENABLE
        help
            Synchronise the wall clock from pool.ntp.org once Wi-Fi is up.
            Without it the time service stays on the DEMO clock.

endmenu

menu "Little World diagnostics (build-time only)"

    # Backlight diagnostics for the panel-flicker comparison builds. The choice
    # is compile-time on purpose: a runtime switch would leave the LEDC timer
    # configured and make some of the runs indistinguishable.
    choice LW_BACKLIGHT_MODE
        prompt "Backlight control (diagnostic)"
        default LW_BACKLIGHT_RUNTIME

        config LW_BACKLIGHT_RUNTIME
            bool "Standard: LEDC duty follows the brightness slider"
            help
                The shipping behaviour: the BSP LEDC channel is rewritten every
                time the brightness preference changes.

        config LW_BACKLIGHT_FIXED
            bool "Fixed duty: write once at boot, never again"
            help
                Diagnostic B. The brightness slider becomes a stored preference
                that never reaches the LEDC channel. If the flicker stops, the
                runtime duty writes are the cause.

        config LW_BACKLIGHT_MINIMAL
            bool "Minimal load: fixed duty at 30%, no runtime writes"
            help
                Diagnostic C. Fixed duty at a low level, so the LCD boost and
                charge pump run at their smallest load.
    endchoice

    config LW_DIAG_STATIC_UI
        bool "Diagnostic C: static UI, no animation or per-frame updates"
        default n
        help
            Freeze the desktop: the sprite frame clock never runs, actors stop
            moving, and the 20 ms OS tick stops refreshing labels. Used only to
            separate "the animation/render load flickers the panel" from "the
            display path itself flickers". Never ship a build with this on.

    config LW_DIAG_NO_MEDIUM
        bool "Diagnostic D: behave as if no TF card were inserted"
        default n
        help
            Skips the card mount entirely and takes the same code path a real
            missing card takes: embedded character pack, labelled scene
            fallback, no scene files. It exists so the no-card acceptance run
            can be done without physically removing the card, and so the
            fallback cannot rot unnoticed. Never ship a build with this on.

endmenu